<title>JAPAN: Sony,Philips develop next-generation optical discs.</title>
<headline>Sony,Philips develop next-generation optical discs.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp said on Monday that it and Philips Electronics NV had jointly developed next-generation optical discs.  </p>
<p>The new optical discs are based on direct-stream digital (DSD) technology which boosts information capacity to four times that of compact discs (CDs), a Sony spokesman said.</p>
<p>The new discs can be played on conventional CD players, he said. It has not been decided when the new discs will hit the market, he said.</p>
